    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "Clarify -ipcbind syntax when using max-connections with the default Unix socket",
    "body": "The -ipcbind option supports the default Unix socket address unix and per-address connection limits using the max-connections option.\n\nThe examples for the connection-limit syntax use -ipcbind=unix:,max-connections=8, with a colon after unix. It may be worth clarifying whether this colon is required when adding socket options to the default Unix socket address.\n\nIs -ipcbind=unix:,max-connections=8 the intended syntax for setting a connection limit on the default socket, and is the colon required to distinguish the socket address from the following options?\n\nIf so, documenting this distinction in the -ipcbind help text could make the syntax easier to understand.\n\nRelated PR\n\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35037\n\nI have not independently tested the alternative syntax. This report is asking for clarification rather than asserting that a confirmed bug exists.",
