      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "`-ipcbind=unix:,max-connections=8` is the intended syntax. Testing both with the colon and without it, the former would bind the default socket to 8 connection slots, while the latter would fail with an unrecognized address error.\n\nThe parser only processes inline options for addresses starting with `unix:`. The empty path after the colon would still select the default socket as it would for `unix`. Bare `unix` works as a shorthand when used without the options.\n\nLooking at this, the parser could be updated to use it without the colon, seeing as `unix` is a valid address. Reasonably speaking, the form without the colon should work. The help text could be further clarified, or the parser could be modified to support it without the colon.",
